    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent my whole life thinking i was destined for something massive. coding, competitions, just constant grinding to be the best. but i just hit this wall. i realized i'm just... average. i'm just another dev. i'll never be a maverick or a legend. honestly, it feels like i've wasted every single second of my life just to end up being nothing special. being mediocre feels like a slow death.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing a very common crisis of expectation, where the difference between \"best\" and \"competent\" feels insurmountable. Remember that \"average\" simply means competent enough to contribute and solve real-world problems. Instead of chasing legendary status, focus on mastering a specific, useful skill and finding genuine satisfaction in your daily work. Your growth and contributions, however small they feel now, are still meaningful.",
