    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just noise. saying it's \"meaningful\" is just something people say to make themselves feel better about being unremarkable. if you know you're never going to reach the peak, why even bother with the struggle? the rest of my life is just going to be this endless, repetitive loop of being \"fine\" and \"useful.\" it's exhausting just thinking about the next forty years of being nobody.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel disillusioned when the massive goals you set don't materialize. However, purpose isn't always tied to legendary achievement; it can be found in the immediate process. Shifting your focus from \"being the best\" to \"getting better by 1%\" every day can transform the grind from an endless loop into a continuous journey of self-improvement. Allow yourself to redefine what success means for *you*, outside of external validation.",
      "source": "target",
